<title>PHILIPPINES: New industrial estate eyed in southern Philippines.</title>
<headline>New industrial estate eyed in southern Philippines.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Philippine real estate developer is planning to build an industrial estate and a leisure resort in a 1,400-hectare site at the southern island of Mindanao, the Board of Investments (BOI) said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The BOI said unlisted Cordova Land Properties would require an estimated 52 billion pesos to develop the Malita Industrial Estate City &amp; Resort in Davao del Sur province.</p>
<p>The project will include an industrial estate, a commercial subdivision, a residential enclave, a resort, a 36-hole golf course, an airport and two seaports.</p>
<p>The BOI said tourism-oriented ventures and transportation facilities are considered priority investment projects.</p>
<p>-- Manila Newsroom (63 2) 841-8938 Fax 817-6267</p>
</text>
